  "treePlacement": {
    "$comment": "PK 1.8.0: where PK's trees grow. forest = the kinds of the map's trees (wood to cut) and how often each grows (weight; 'bamboo' would keep the built-in bamboo clump: left out, its low-poly shape did not sit with PK's trees). village = every house (houseTypes) in a group of at least minHouses (houses within linkM m of each other count as one group) has a coconut palm and a banana plant in its yard (PK: houses of three or more always have them). wayside = now and then (share of the tiles) a palm or a coconut beside the worn paths (wear above worn, the tree's own tile below clear) within radius m of a storehouse (PK: along the working way to the ឃ្លាំង). Each tree is scaled to its `height` (m) unless its crown would then be wider than `width` (m): the map's forests stand a tree a tile (2 m), so the crowns are kept to the size of the built-in trees they replace. nearTris = how many triangles the detailed models may take at once (the RTS view, the 3D hero mode): the nearest trees get PK's model itself (`hi` triangles, scripts/models/trees.mjs); every other tree is drawn as crossed picture cards of the same model (`cards`: 6 side views and 2 from above, baked by scripts/models/grassCards.mjs ... turn 0 top; `card` = the picture's size when the tree is 1 tall), 8 triangles a tree, so a whole forest keeps its detail and the frame budget. confidence: GAMEPLAY_ABSTRACTION (coconut and banana in Khmer house yards are an everyday sight; the exact rule is the game's).",
